'''Health and environment'''
*[[2026 Ebola epidemic]]
**A case of [[Ebola]] is reported in the [[Sud-Ubangi]] [[Provinces of the Democratic Republic of the Congo|province]], making it the seventh province in the [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]] the outbreak has spread to. [https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/africa/ebola-congo-outbreak-spreads-b3048824.html (''The Independent'')] 
*[[2026 United States cyclosporiasis outbreak]]
**The [[Food and Drug Administration|U.S. Food and Drug Administration]] and [[Centers for Disease Control and Prevention|U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention]] declares an end to the [[cyclosporiasis]] food poisoning outbreak, which is caused by ''[[cyclospora cayetanensis]]'' and linked to [[iceberg lettuce]] from [[Taylor Farms]], in the [[United States]]. [https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/11/cdc-record-cyclosporiasis-outbreak-over.html (CNBC)] [https://www.reuters.com/business/healthcare-pharmaceuticals/us-declares-end-largest-recorded-cyclosporiasis-outbreak-2026-09-11/ (Reuters)]
*[[Endangerment of orangutans]], [[India–Indonesia relations]]
**[[Indonesia]] works with [[India]]n authorities to repatriate five baby [[orangutan]]s found in an [[Odisha]] [[Forests in Odisha|forest]] after suspected [[Wildlife smuggling|trafficking]]. [[Odisha Police]] and India's [[Wildlife Crime Control Bureau]] examine how the apes, which are native to [[Borneo]] and [[Sumatra]], reached India. [https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260911-indonesia-to-bring-back-baby-orangutans-allegedly-trafficked-to-india (AFP via France 24)]
*[[Health effects arising from the September 11 attacks]]
**A research study at the [[Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai|Icahn School of Medicine]] at [[Mount Sinai Health System|Mount Sinai]] reports that, in the [[Aftermath of the September 11 attacks|aftermath]] of the [[September 11 attacks]], [[World Trade Center (1973–2001)|World Trade Center]] responders living in greener neighborhoods had lower risks of frailty, [[Post-traumatic stress disorder|PTSD]], and [[Major depressive disorder|depression]]. Greater exposure to heat and air pollution was associated with higher risks of these conditions. [https://abcnews.com/Health/residential-air-pollution-linked-higher-depression-scores-911/story?id=136361763 (ABC News)] [https://www.mountsinai.org/about/newsroom/2026/25-years-after-9-11-study-finds-neighborhood-environment-may-influence-frailty-ptsd-and-depression-risk-among-world-trade-center-responders (Mount Sinai)]

